UNAME(2)                       P32W Unix                        UNAME(2)

NAME
       uname - get the system's name

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/utsname.h>

       int uname(struct utsname *u);

DESCRIPTION
       uname fills *u with five NUL-terminated strings of up to 31
       characters:

           struct utsname {
               char sysname[32];     "P32W Unix"
               char nodename[32];    "p32w"
               char release[32];     "0.7"
               char version[32];     "M7"
               char machine[32];     "p32w"
           };

       The strings are fixed in the kernel.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success; -1 on an error, with errno set.

ERRORS
       EFAULT  u is a bad address.

EXAMPLES
       struct utsname un;
       uname(&un);
       printf("%s %s\n", un.sysname, un.release);

SEE ALSO
       uname(1)

BUGS
       The node name cannot be set.
